// prompts.memql
//
// Authoring-namespace prompt declarations for the planner's design/repair
// loop (epic memql#954, issue #960). Bodies live in prompts/<name>.tmpl.
//
// authoringDesign is the DESIGN PASS: given a natural-language Responsibility
// and a summary of the caller's reusable catalog, it decomposes the
// Responsibility into the dependency closure a v1:authoring:bundle needs --
// the headline automation plus each supporting construct -- and emits a
// candidate `.memql` source SKETCH per dependency. The planner's Go side
// (agent_loop_authoring.go) keys each sketch through the deterministic +
// fuzzy catalog matchers (DecideReuse / CatalogNearMatches, #957) to decide
// reuse-or-author per dependency. The model proposes; the engine matches.

/// Authoring DESIGN PASS (epic #954, #960). Decomposes a natural-language Responsibility into the
/// dependency closure a planner-authored bundle needs: the headline automation plus each supporting
/// construct (query / mutation / logic / spec / trait / shape), with a candidate .memql source
/// sketch per dependency that the deterministic + fuzzy catalog matchers key for the
/// reuse-or-author decision. Sonnet, not Opus: the workload is grounded decomposition against a
/// known catalog + construct grammar, not novel chain-of-thought. The model proposes candidate
/// constructs; the planner's Go side runs the actual reuse-or-author math (DecideReuse /
/// CatalogNearMatches) -- so the model must NOT claim a construct is reused, only describe the
/// construct it needs. Output contract: {automationName, automationPurpose, dependencies: [{kind,
/// name, purpose, candidateSource}]}. kind in {query, mutation, logic, spec, trait, shape}.
/// candidateSource is a self-contained .memql sketch of ONE construct of that kind.
@defaultProvider("streamClaudeSonnet")
@templateFile("prompts/authoringDesign.tmpl")
prompt authoringDesign {
  responsibility  string! @description("The user's standing Responsibility in natural language -- the duty the authored bundle must fulfill. The single most important input; the dependency closure is decomposed from it.")
  catalog         []object           @description("Summary of the caller's reusable catalog -- [{name, kind}] of constructs already promoted for reuse (#957). The model uses this to PREFER describing a dependency that matches an existing catalog entry (so the matcher reuses it) over inventing a novel one. Empty when the owner has no catalog yet.")
  now             string! @description("RFC3339 wall-clock at invocation. Lets the design reason about time-relative triggers/schedules without hardcoding a clock.")
}

// authoringEmit is the EMISSION PASS (#960 increment 2): given the design pass'
// resolved plan -- the headline automation, the dependencies to AUTHOR (with
// their candidate sketches), and the REAL names of the dependencies being
// REUSED from the catalog -- it emits the final, compiling `.memql` source for
// each authored construct plus the automation. Grounded so it references the
// reused construct names verbatim (no hallucinated symbols). Output is fed
// straight into Gate 1 (the isolated compile-and-bind harness).

/// Authoring EMISSION PASS (epic #954, #960). Renders the design pass' resolved plan into the final
/// compiling .memql source for a bundle: the headline automation plus every AUTHORED member
/// construct, grounded so it references the REAL names of the REUSED catalog constructs verbatim
/// (no hallucinated symbols). Sonnet, not Opus: structured rendering against a fixed grammar + a
/// resolved plan, not novel reasoning. Hard rule baked into the prompt: NEVER emit @shape or
/// @enabled on a spec (Gate 1 + the live spec loader both reject them). Output contract:
/// {constructs: [{kind, name, source}]}. kind in {automation, query, mutation, logic, spec, trait,
/// shape}. source is the self-contained, compilable .memql for ONE construct.
@defaultProvider("streamClaudeSonnet")
@templateFile("prompts/authoringEmit.tmpl")
prompt authoringEmit {
  responsibility    string! @description("The originating Responsibility, carried through for grounding so the emitted constructs stay faithful to the user's intent.")
  automationName    string! @description("The headline automation name the design pass chose -- emit one automation construct under this name.")
  automationPurpose string             @description("One-line description of what the automation does, for the @description annotation.")
  authored          []object           @description("The dependencies to AUTHOR net-new -- [{kind, name, purpose, candidateSource}]. Emit a compiling construct for each, refining the candidateSource sketch into valid, bindable .memql.")
  reused            []object           @description("The dependencies being REUSED from the catalog -- [{name, kind, namespace}]. Do NOT author these; reference them by their real name where the automation / authored constructs need them, and `use` them from their namespace.")
  now               string! @description("RFC3339 wall-clock at invocation.")
}

// authoringRepair is the REPAIR PASS (#960 increment 2): when Gate 1 rejects
// one or more emitted constructs, this prompt takes the failing constructs plus
// their compile/bind diagnostics and re-emits CORRECTED source for only those
// constructs. The planner re-runs Gate 1 on the spliced bundle and repeats,
// bounded by a hard repair-attempt cap + the planner's cumulative LLM ceiling.

/// Authoring REPAIR PASS (epic #954, #960). Given the Gate-1 diagnostics for a set of failing
/// constructs, re-emits CORRECTED .memql source for ONLY those constructs so the bundle recompiles.
/// Sonnet: targeted error-driven correction against the same grammar as the emit pass. Same hard
/// rule: NEVER emit @shape or @enabled on a spec. Output contract: {constructs: [{kind, name,
/// source}]} -- the corrected versions keyed by the same (kind, name) so the planner splices them
/// back into the bundle. May add a missing construct a diagnostic revealed.
@defaultProvider("streamClaudeSonnet")
@templateFile("prompts/authoringRepair.tmpl")
prompt authoringRepair {
  responsibility  string! @description("The originating Responsibility, for grounding.")
  automationName  string             @description("The bundle's headline automation name, for context.")
  failing         []object! @description("The constructs Gate 1 rejected -- [{kind, name, source}]. Re-emit a corrected version for each.")
  diagnostics     []object! @description("The per-construct Gate-1 compile/bind failures -- [{kind, name, error}]. The error is the exact diagnostic to fix; address it precisely rather than rewriting from scratch.")
  now             string! @description("RFC3339 wall-clock at invocation.")
}
